.SH "BUGS"
Debug output is unconditionally enabled by \fBrecord\.debug = True\fR at module level and cannot be suppressed via the \fBRECORD_DEBUG\fR environment variable\.
.P
\fBbasename\fR is used in debug output but is never imported from \fBos\.path\fR\. All debug \fBsys\.stderr\.write\fR calls that reference \fBbasename(sys\.argv[0])\fR will raise a \fBNameError\fR at runtime whenever debug mode is active\.
.P
The \fBtable_parameter\fR regex is applied with \fB\.match(arg)\fR without first checking whether the result is \fBNone\fR; any argument that does not match the \fB\-\-table=\fR pattern will cause an \fBAttributeError\fR on \fB\.groups()\fR\. The same issue exists in the column\-parsing loop for \fBcolumn_parameter\.match(arg)\fR\.
.P
The bare \fBexcept: raise\fR in the column validation block swallows the original exception context, making it harder to diagnose unexpected database errors\.
.P
The \fBexcept: raise\fR in the \fBsearch\fR call similarly loses the original traceback context\.
.P
The \fBparameters\fR function verifies column existence by executing a schema query once per column argument rather than once per table, making it potentially slow for tables with many columns and many filter arguments\.
.P
The PostgreSQL column existence check uses \fBinformation_schema\.columns\fR without filtering by schema name, which may return false positives if multiple schemas contain tables with the same name\.
.P
The \fBtarget\fR variable is assigned inside the Gremlin branch when \fBcol_argument is None\fR, but is never used anywhere in the function, suggesting incomplete implementation of the target\-column selection logic for the Gremlin backend\.
.P
The \fB__license__\fR string contains a stray capital \fBG\fR in the word \fBthat\fR (\fB"in the hope thaGt it will be useful"\fR)\.
